      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T14:07:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a box edge a few ulps longer than whole cells gets no extra column\n\nDexel::block and the field block's gate counted cells with a plain ceiling. A box edge\nread back from a rigid move is often a few ulps long: 12.7 mm two ulps long over 0.254 is\n50 plus about 1e-14, so the grid got 51 columns. The last one is a few femtometres wide\ninside the box, and the stock top stands in it a whole cell past the box edge\n(Stock::top 0.1 mm outside the box returns the stock top). A caller that meshes the\ngrid to the box edge gets a row of zero-width cells: every facet in it collapses when\ncorners within 1e-8 mm are welded, and the row's edges carry six facets.\n\ncells_across(extent, cell) is the ceiling, except that an extent within 1e-9 (relative)\nof a whole number of cells is that number. Both arms' gates use it, so they still count\nthe same columns. It is public so a caller that sizes its own grid to the stock counts\nthe same way.\n\nPins (cell_count_tests.rs, all three fail on the plain ceiling: 51 against 50):\n- the count of a whole number of cells up to rounding, and of a real part cell;\n- no material past a box edge read a few ulps long;\n- 4096 cells a few ulps long are inside the ceiling, not refused as 4097.\n\nRefs #4012\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
