      "committer": {
        "name": "dylanoliverdo-coder",
        "email": "265406556+dylanoliverdo-coder@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T14:07:06Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the exact carry read counts the block's columns; a thin box keeps its column\n\nReview fixes to the cell count:\n- History::read (carry_exact.rs) sized the same box with its own plain ceiling, so after\n  a side or lattice turn the read gave 51 columns where Dexel::block gave 50, and the\n  sliver came back. It now uses cells_across.\n- An extent under 1e-9 of a cell rounded to 0 columns and was refused. It now falls back\n  to the ceiling, one column, as before.\n\nPins: the carry read keeps the block's 50 columns (fails with the read's old ceiling:\n51); a 1e-10 mm box gets one column. cell_count tests 4 passed, clippy clean.\n\nFixes #4012\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
